+Production DL Hardware & Scale - operator checklist
+
+1) Provision validated hardware pools
+ - Create dedicated self-hosted runner fleets for GPU/TPU/NPUs; follow ops/hw/ci/runner_provision/harden_runner.sh to harden.
+ - For each vendor (Inferentia, Graphcore, Habana), run the corresponding smoke scripts in ops/hw/validation to confirm runtime availability.
+
+2) Autoscaling & preemption handling
+ - Use spot/spot-like node pools for cost-sensitive workloads; annotate workloads using nodeSelector/tolerations as in ops/dl/production/k8s_preemptible_job.yaml.
+ - Ensure containers include a preemption handler (ops/dl/production/spot_preemption_handler.sh) to upload checkpoints on SIGTERM.
+ - Integrate cluster autoscaler / Karpenter (example app scaffold) for scale-to-zero and scale-up responses.
+
+3) Checkpointing & resume
+ - Use ops/multimodal/scale/checkpoint_uploader.py for periodic uploads to S3 from training loops.
+ - Use ops/dl/production/checkpoint_manager.py (see repo examples) in training to find latest checkpoint and resume.
+
+4) Data sharding & shard-local IO
+ - Shard datasets with ops/dl/production/data_sharder.py and use WebDataset or shard-aware dataloaders for high throughput.
+
+5) RLHF & large-model scaffolding
+ - Use DeepSpeed or torch.distributed with ZeRO stage configs (ops/dl/distributed/deepspeed_config.json) to enable sharded optimizer states and memory savings.
+ - Orchestrate RLHF stages via Argo (ops/dl/rlhf/argo_rlhf_workflow.yaml) and ensure checkpoints between stages.
+
+6) Monitoring, SLOs & alerts
+ - Deploy Prometheus rules (ops/monitoring/prometheus/training_rules.yml) and Grafana dashboard (ops/monitoring/grafana/training_dashboard.json).
+ - Configure Alertmanager receivers and escalation policies for TrainingJobStuck and cost alerts.
+
+7) CI & gating
+ - Ensure hardware builds run on secure self-hosted runners and require cosign signing & Rekor entries (prior patches).
+ - Validate runners regularly using .github/workflows/validate_runner_drivers.yml.
+
